y partially accurate: the target explicitly flags the idempotence question as open, but flagging an open question about a property of the construction is not the same as failing to preserve the guarantees the construction is designed to enforce. The guarantees are preserved by the acceptance policy (grounded-extension membership with guarantee-violation attacks), not by idempotence per se.\n\nAccordingly, the critic has not established that the target fails to deliver a complete, guarantee-preserving proposal. The target specifies a determinate acceptance semantics, preserves guarantees by construction, and acknowledges an open structural question whose resolution is not required for the guarantees to hold."}